14.1 Glossary
A
Accuracy — Chance to hit a target; influenced by range, elevation, suppression.

Afterburner — Temporary speed boost for air units; drains energy.

AI Personality — Behavioral profile that shapes squad decision‑making.

Altitude Bands — Vertical layers determining air combat behavior.

B
Breach — Autonomous CQB entry maneuver involving stack, suppress, and clear phases.

Build Radius — Area where buildings can be constructed.

C
Command Core — Primary HQ; generates tokens, radius, and strategic abilities.

Command Radius — Area where squads receive bonuses and improved coordination.

Command Tokens — Strategic currency used for intents, abilities, logistics, and experimental actions.

Cover — Terrain or objects that reduce incoming damage and suppression.

D
Depth Layers — Vertical zones for naval units (surface, mid, deep).

Destructible Cover — Cover that can be destroyed by weapons or hazards.

E
Elevation — Height advantage affecting visibility, accuracy, and range.

Experimental Units — Unique units with special rules and superweapon abilities.

F
Flanking — Autonomous maneuver to attack from side or rear.

Fog‑of‑War — Hidden areas of the map; influenced by sensors and elevation.

G
Gravity Well — Experimental ability that distorts movement and terrain.

H
Hazard Zone — Fire, radiation, EMP, or toxic areas affecting units.

I
Initiative — Determines action order in combat cycles.

Intent — High‑level command directive interpreted by autonomous squads.

L
Logistics Node — Structure that routes resources and coordinates repairs.

M
Morale — Squad confidence; affects accuracy, retreat likelihood, and cohesion.

P
Payload — Weapons and munitions carried by a unit.

Penetration — Ability to bypass armor.

R
Range Bands — Discrete engagement distances (melee, short, medium, long, extreme).

Repair Drones — Autonomous drones that repair buildings and units.

S
Sensor Suite — LIDAR, thermal, radar systems used for detection.

Shields — Energy barriers that absorb damage before HP.

Suppression — Heavy fire that reduces movement, accuracy, and morale.

T
Tech Tree — Progression system unlocking units, upgrades, and abilities.

Torpedo Lane — Naval path where torpedoes travel; dangerous for subs.

V
Vector Core — Experimental command unit enabling teleportation and superweapons.

Visibility Cone — Directional sightline determining what a unit can see.

VR Operator Mode — First‑person tactical support mode.

VR Dogfight Mode — Full cockpit air combat integrated with RTS.

