14.3 Quick‑Start Guide
This section teaches new players how to begin playing Obsidian Protocol in under 2 minutes.

Step 1 — Build Your Command Core
Your Command Core establishes:

Command radius

Token generation

Strategic abilities

Tech tree access

Place it in a safe, elevated, defensible location.

Step 2 — Establish Economy
Build:

Resource extractors

Logistics nodes

Fusion (power grid)

Research lab

Your economy determines your long‑term strength.

Step 3 — Deploy Initial Squads
Recommended starting squads:

1 Recon unit

2 Infantry squads

1 Light vehicle

1 Air recon drone

These units secure early map control.

Step 4 — Issue Intents
Use the Command Wheel to issue:

Recon intent

Hold intent

Assault intent

Squads interpret intent autonomously.

Step 5 — Expand Command Radius
Build:

Nexus

Insight

This increases coordination and visibility.

Step 6 — Unlock Tech Tree
Choose a branch:

Tactical

Strategic

Logistics

Experimental

Your tech tree defines your faction identity.

Step 7 — Use VR Mode (Optional)
Jump into:

Recon drones

Air units

Operator mode

VR enhances tactical precision.

Step 8 — Push Objectives
Capture:

Command zones

Resource nodes

Strategic terrain

Complete objectives to earn VP.

Step 9 — Deploy Experimental Units
Late‑game power spikes:

Echo

Nullpoint

Specter

Phantom

Helix

These units reshape the battlefield.

Step 10 — Win Conditions
Achieve victory by:

VP threshold

Command Core destruction

Superweapon deployment

Campaign completion

